{
  "id": "Compound::DB00318 - Gene::1576",
  "verbalization": "Codeine's interaction with Cyp3a4 appears to be mediated through a series of interconnected pathways involving opioid receptor activation and enzyme induction. The evidence suggests that Codeine, through its effects on opioid receptors, may indirectly influence Cyp3a4 expression or activity. In one pathway, Codeine binds to Ugt2b4, which is part of the Farnesoid X Receptor (FXR) pathway, ultimately leading to Cyp3a4 participation. In another pathway, Codeine causes ureteral spasms, which are mediated by Hydrocodone, a related opioid, and this chain of events leads to Cyp3a4 binding. The shared involvement of opioid receptor agonists in both pathways highlights a potential mechanism by which Codeine and its related compounds may modulate Cyp3a4 activity. The integration of these pathways suggests that Codeine's effects on Cyp3a4 are likely dependent on the activation of opioid receptors, which in turn may influence metabolic enzymes through receptor-mediated signaling or transcriptional regulation.",
